---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { profile } from "../../data/profile";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy and analytics | Eero Siivola"
  description="How analytics consent and privacy choices are handled on Eero Siivola's website."
>
  <header class="evidence-hero">
    <div class="shell evidence-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy and analytics.</h1>
      </div>
      <p>
        This page describes the limited information this professional website stores and how
        optional analytics consent works.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section narrative-section">
    <div class="shell prose privacy-copy">
      <h2>Current data collection</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no accounts, contact forms, advertising, or personalised marketing. Google
        Analytics is configured with measurement ID <code>G-RK8VRLQ1ND</code>, but its tag does not
        load until you explicitly allow analytics.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Google Analytics is used to understand aggregate site traffic and which pages are useful.
        Its default measurement can include session statistics, approximate location, and browser
        and device information. The Google tag is blocked unless you select
        <strong>Allow analytics</strong>. Selecting <strong>Decline analytics</strong> prevents it
        from loading and sends no consent or measurement request to Google.
      </p>
      <p>
        Advertising storage, advertising user data, and advertising personalisation remain denied
        in both cases. Google describes its handling of information in the{" "}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Embedded LinkedIn video</h2>
      <p>
        Some pages feature short videos published on LinkedIn. These are embedded directly from
        <code>linkedin.com</code>, so loading one lets LinkedIn set its own cookies and collect data
        about your visit, including tracking that may be linked to a LinkedIn account. Because this
        is third-party tracking, no video loads until you allow it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Until you allow embedded video, each video shows a placeholder in its place with a short
        explanation. You can allow it there, or under <strong>Embedded video</strong> in privacy
        settings; you can also open any video directly on LinkedIn without allowing it here. Allowing
        embedded video means you acknowledge that LinkedIn may collect data and track you under its
        own terms, described in the{" "}
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy">LinkedIn Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Declining, or later changing your choice to declined, stops further videos from loading.
        Cookies that LinkedIn already set through a video you had loaded are governed by LinkedIn and
        can be cleared through your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Your saved choices</h2>
      <p>
        The site stores your choices in your browser's local storage: your analytics choice under
        <code>eero-analytics-consent-v1</code> and your embedded-video choice under
        <code>eero-media-consent-v1</code>. Each strictly necessary value records only
        <code>granted</code> or <code>denied</code>. Neither is sent to Eero, Google, or LinkedIn.
      </p>
      <button class="privacy-settings-button" type="button" data-open-consent-settings hidden>
        Change privacy settings
      </button>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Links to LinkedIn, GitHub, Google Scholar, ORCID, Vuono Group, and publication services
        take you to those organisations' websites. Their own privacy practices apply after you
        follow a link.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this site's privacy implementation can be sent through{" "}
        <a href={profile.social.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-copy h2 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
  }

  .privacy-copy h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .privacy-copy code {
    padding: 0.12rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .privacy-settings-button {
    min-height: 46px;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: transparent;
    font-weight: 750;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .privacy-settings-button:hover {
    color: var(--paper);
    background: var(--ink);
  }

  .privacy-settings-button[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
